{
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "time": {
    "from": "now-1h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "timezone": "",
  "title": "Oja Connect: Agent Observability",
  "uid": "oja-agent-obs",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "tags": [
    "oja-connect",
    "adk",
    "gen_ai",
    "issue-11"
  ],
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "model",
        "label": "Model",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "query": {
          "query": "label_values(gen_ai_request_model)",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        "refresh": 2,
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true,
        "allValue": ".*",
        "current": {
          "text": "All",
          "value": "$__all"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "conversation",
        "type": "textbox",
        "label": "Conversation id",
        "query": ".*",
        "current": {
          "text": ".*",
          "value": ".*"
        },
        "options": [
          {
            "text": ".*",
            "value": ".*",
            "selected": true
          }
        ],
        "hide": 0,
        "description": "Paste a gen_ai.conversation.id (the AG-UI threadId) to see just that conversation's turns. Leave as .* to see all."
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 100,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Source:** ADK computes these `gen_ai.*` metrics natively; the backend `MeterProvider` (issue #11) exports them via the collector to Prometheus. Panels may show **No data** until the in-code instrumentation follow-up runs and real traffic exists. **Metric-name caveat:** the OTLP->Prometheus exporter may append a unit suffix (durations become `..._seconds_*`, token counts may become `..._tokens_*`). If a panel is empty, open the Prometheus metric browser and adjust the suffix. Cache-read tokens are a **span attribute** in ADK, not part of the native token-usage metric, so the cache-ratio and cached-token series depend on the follow-up recording them as a metric (see panel notes)."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "1. Context cache hit ratio (cache_read / input)",
      "description": "Proves context caching is working live. ADK's native token-usage metric only splits input/output; cache_read is a span attribute. The follow-up must record cache_read tokens as a metric (token.type=\"cache_read\" or a dedicated oja.* histogram). Query below assumes token.type=cache_read is emitted.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(oja_llm_cached_input_tokens_sum[$__rate_interval])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(oja_llm_input_tokens_sum[$__rate_interval])), 1)",
          "legendFormat": "cache hit ratio"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "2. Tokens in / out / cached over time, by model",
      "description": "gen_ai.client.token.usage split by gen_ai.token.type and gen_ai.request.model. 'cached' depends on the follow-up emitting token.type=cache_read.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "IN",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (model) (rate(oja_llm_input_tokens_sum{model=~\"$model\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "input - {{gen_ai_request_model}}"
        },
        {
          "refId": "OUT",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (model) (rate(oja_llm_output_tokens_sum{model=~\"$model\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "output - {{gen_ai_request_model}}"
        },
        {
          "refId": "CACHE",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (model) (rate(oja_llm_cached_input_tokens_sum{model=~\"$model\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "cached - {{gen_ai_request_model}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "3. Estimated cost over time (USD, DERIVED)",
      "description": "OTel semconv has NO cost attribute (see #11); this is our derived number from estimate_cost_usd(). The follow-up records it as the metric oja_llm_cost_usd. Not a billing source of truth.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 13
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "currencyUSD"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (gen_ai_request_model) (rate(oja_llm_cost_usd_sum{gen_ai_request_model=~\"$model\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "$/s - {{gen_ai_request_model}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "4a. Estimated cost per turn (USD, DERIVED)",
      "description": "Mean derived cost per agent turn = rate(oja_llm_cost_usd_sum)/rate(oja_llm_cost_usd_count). Depends on the follow-up.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 13
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "currencyUSD",
          "decimals": 5
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "colorMode": "value"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(oja_llm_cost_usd_sum[$__rate_interval])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(oja_llm_cost_usd_count[$__rate_interval])), 1)",
          "legendFormat": "cost/turn"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "4b. Inference calls per agent turn (did it re-plan?)",
      "description": "gen_ai.invoke_agent.inference_calls histogram. Mean = rate(sum)/rate(count). A rising line means the agent is making multiple model calls per turn (re-planning / tool-loop).",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 13
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(gen_ai_invoke_agent_inference_calls_sum[$__rate_interval])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(gen_ai_invoke_agent_inference_calls_count[$__rate_interval])), 1)",
          "legendFormat": "avg inference calls/turn"
        },
        {
          "refId": "P95",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(gen_ai_invoke_agent_inference_calls_bucket[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95 inference calls/turn"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "5. Tool calls per turn",
      "description": "gen_ai.invoke_agent.tool_calls histogram. Mean and p95 tool calls per agent invocation.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 21
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(gen_ai_invoke_agent_tool_calls_sum[$__rate_interval])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(gen_ai_invoke_agent_tool_calls_count[$__rate_interval])), 1)",
          "legendFormat": "avg tool calls/turn"
        },
        {
          "refId": "P95",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(gen_ai_invoke_agent_tool_calls_bucket[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95 tool calls/turn"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "6. Tool exec p95 & workflow duration (seconds)",
      "description": "gen_ai.execute_tool.duration and gen_ai.invoke_workflow.duration histograms. Durations may export with a _seconds suffix; adjust if empty.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 21
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "TOOLP95",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(gen_ai_execute_tool_duration_seconds_bucket[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "tool exec p95"
        },
        {
          "refId": "WFP95",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(gen_ai_invoke_workflow_duration_seconds_bucket[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "workflow p95"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "7. Slow or high-token traces (Tempo / TraceQL)",
      "description": "Structural TraceQL. Click a row to open the trace, then jump to its Loki content via trace-to-logs. Edit the query for your threshold.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "tempo",
        "uid": "tempo"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 29
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "tempo",
            "uid": "tempo"
          },
          "queryType": "traceql",
          "query": "{ span.gen_ai.usage.output_tokens > 1000 || duration > 3s }",
          "limit": 20,
          "tableType": "traces"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 101,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "8. Conversations: turns grouped by conversation id",
      "description": "Each row is ONE agent turn (one buyer message). The Conversation-id column is gen_ai.conversation.id (the AG-UI threadId); turns that share it are the same conversation. Paste an id into the Conversation-id dashboard variable to drill into a single conversation, or leave it .* to see every recent conversation. Click a row to open that turn's trace, then follow trace-to-logs into the prompt/response in Loki. This is per-conversation observability entirely in the Grafana stack (Langfuse is only a plus). see #11",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "tempo",
        "uid": "tempo"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 39
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "tempo",
            "uid": "tempo"
          },
          "queryType": "traceql",
          "query": "{ span.gen_ai.conversation.id =~ \"$conversation\" } | select(span.gen_ai.conversation.id, span.gen_ai.agent.name)",
          "limit": 50,
          "tableType": "traces"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}